          "text": "Description: On May 28, 2009, between 4:25 and 4:50 AM, two witnesses observed a static and particularly bright point in the sky. Photos were taken of the phenomenon, whose brightness dimmed with the dawn. These witnesses likely made an astronomical observation of Jupiter, which is particularly visible during this time of year (apparent magnitude approximately -2.5 and angular diameter approximately 40\").",
